WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:04.100
[The D Dorm]

3
00:04.830 --> 00:06.640
Your wound has dried up.

4
00:06.660 --> 00:08.780
- Ow... - You don't need a Band-Aid anymore.

5
00:09.120 --> 00:09.830
By the way...

6
00:10.320 --> 00:11.300
does it still hurt?

7
00:12.130 --> 00:12.890
Ow, hey!

8
00:21.670 --> 00:23.620
Your eyes meet...

9
00:23.630 --> 00:25.540
gazing at each other.

10
00:25.540 --> 00:27.250
Something sensual.

11
00:27.250 --> 00:28.240
Sensual...

12
00:28.240 --> 00:30.040
Sensual, sensual...

13
00:33.710 --> 00:34.710
When will you let go?

14
00:34.730 --> 00:35.580
Oh...

15
00:40.180 --> 00:41.120
You're so weak.

16
00:41.120 --> 00:43.060
That was just a small poke, but you yelped like you were crushed.

17
00:44.170 --> 00:45.370
What kind of sane person

18
00:45.550 --> 00:46.900
pokes other people's wounds?

19
00:47.030 --> 00:48.300
Is your hand even clean?

20
00:48.980 --> 00:50.550
Just know that it's cleaner than your mouth.

21
00:51.560 --> 00:53.410
Don't ask me to tend your wounds next time, then.

22
00:55.180 --> 00:55.990
Come on...

23
00:56.000 --> 00:56.630
Oh,

24
00:56.940 --> 00:57.980
by the way...

25
00:58.100 --> 01:00.650
you two seem to get along well.

26
01:00.950 --> 01:02.960
You bicker back and forth.

27
01:02.960 --> 01:04.700
They say couples like you

28
01:04.700 --> 01:05.770
end up having a bunch of kids.

29
01:06.040 --> 01:06.660
Be quiet,

30
01:06.660 --> 01:07.310
Grandpa.

31
01:07.310 --> 01:08.170
Be quiet about what?

32
01:08.820 --> 01:10.630
I haven't said anything yet, are you insane?

33
01:10.660 --> 01:11.960
Uh...

34
01:12.160 --> 01:13.289
Grandpa has been quiet...

35
01:13.310 --> 01:15.110
He hasn't come into my dreams lately.

36
01:16.070 --> 01:17.030
Well...

37
01:17.030 --> 01:19.020
I have a lot of things I want to ask him.

38
01:19.020 --> 01:20.030
By the way...

39
01:20.039 --> 01:21.050
let me ask you.

40
01:24.620 --> 01:25.630
Take a look at this.

41
01:27.039 --> 01:28.940
Does Grandpa have a lot of these photos?

42
01:29.130 --> 01:31.140
And did he go to Nakhon Sawan often?

43
01:31.950 --> 01:32.740
I can't see it.

44
01:32.740 --> 01:33.509
You can't?

45
01:33.509 --> 01:33.900
Here.

46
01:34.460 --> 01:35.160
Too close!

47
01:35.160 --> 01:36.539
Ugh...who can see from that distance?

48
01:36.590 --> 01:37.840
From wherever you can see it, then.

49
01:40.979 --> 01:41.990
Well...

50
01:42.120 --> 01:44.700
He visited Nakhon Sawan every two or three months.

51
01:46.820 --> 01:49.500
Gramps probably missed you and your mother a lot.

52
01:52.310 --> 01:54.080
But...there are more photos.

53
01:55.020 --> 01:56.360
I think they're kept in the safe.

54
01:56.360 --> 01:58.990
He keeps everything important in there.

55
01:59.720 --> 02:01.220
Wow...

56
02:01.510 --> 02:06.020
Did Grandpa miss my mom that much?

57
02:06.150 --> 02:08.289
I already told you,

58
02:08.300 --> 02:10.570
I just want to see your mother's face.

59
02:11.410 --> 02:12.470
If she were not so stubborn

60
02:12.480 --> 02:15.060
and married the man I chose, she would be better off by now.

61
02:15.230 --> 02:16.940
She would not have to fry rice

62
02:16.940 --> 02:18.740
to repay the bank loans.

63
02:19.420 --> 02:21.800
You're as stubborn as a mule too, Grandpa.

64
02:23.240 --> 02:24.280
Hey...

65
02:25.100 --> 02:26.100
did you talk to yourself?

66
02:26.130 --> 02:26.790
Are you insane?

67
02:26.829 --> 02:27.370
Huh?

68
02:28.060 --> 02:29.280
I was mumbling to the photo.

69
02:29.500 --> 02:30.420
It reminds me of the past

70
02:30.420 --> 02:32.170
since I haven't seen this photo in a long time...

71
02:32.340 --> 02:33.579
You're unhinged.

72
02:33.579 --> 02:34.420
I'm leaving.

73
02:34.420 --> 02:35.400
- Mm... - You're weird.

74
02:35.770 --> 02:36.579
- Whoa! - What...

75
02:37.710 --> 02:38.380
What's wrong? What?

76
02:38.380 --> 02:39.160
What are you?

77
02:39.160 --> 02:39.670
Huh?

78
02:39.960 --> 02:40.570
Ugh...

79
02:40.840 --> 02:41.840
Hey...

80
02:42.500 --> 02:43.390
I'm Dax.

81
02:43.800 --> 02:44.660
This is Dax.

82
02:46.070 --> 02:46.790
Dax?

83
02:46.990 --> 02:48.300
Why are you dressed like that?

84
02:48.300 --> 02:49.350
Why didn't you get changed?

85
02:49.490 --> 02:50.390
Well, last night,

86
02:50.390 --> 02:51.820
we finished filming very late.

87
02:51.820 --> 02:53.050
- Today, I had an early call. - Mm.

88
02:53.060 --> 02:54.530
- Tomorrow, too. - Oh.

89
02:54.540 --> 02:55.820
So I decided to keep this on.

90
02:56.020 --> 02:57.030
I don't wanna change anymore.

91
02:57.370 --> 02:58.540
Whoa, the schedule is pretty tight.

92
02:58.710 --> 03:00.080
Can I sleep in your room tonight?

93
03:00.400 --> 03:00.970
What?

94
03:01.280 --> 03:02.660
I already gave you a room on the third floor, though.

95
03:02.660 --> 03:03.370
Why don't you sleep there?

96
03:03.370 --> 03:04.080
Ugh...

97
03:04.080 --> 03:05.460
Who could fall asleep like that?

98
03:05.480 --> 03:07.430
The next room is drinking and making a racket.

99
03:07.590 --> 03:08.320
Which room is it?

100
03:12.740 --> 03:13.400
Whoa!

101
03:13.400 --> 03:13.870
Sheesh...

102
03:13.870 --> 03:14.670
Hear that?

103
03:15.080 --> 03:16.490
They're this loud?

104
03:16.570 --> 03:17.770
Oh, they're very loud, huh?

105
03:23.010 --> 03:26.560
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

106
03:26.560 --> 03:30.820
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

107
03:32.800 --> 03:38.660
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

108
03:40.030 --> 03:44.760
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

109
03:47.079 --> 03:53.320
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

110
03:54.260 --> 03:58.810
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

111
03:58.829 --> 04:02.410
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

112
04:02.410 --> 04:06.000
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

113
04:06.000 --> 04:09.560
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

114
04:09.570 --> 04:12.000
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

115
04:12.020 --> 04:18.920
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

116
04:18.950 --> 04:26.150
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

117
04:26.150 --> 04:33.350
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

118
04:33.350 --> 04:40.470
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫

119
04:40.490 --> 04:44.360
[The D Dorm]

120
04:59.370 --> 05:01.140
Your solo sounds like you're asking for trouble.

121
05:01.250 --> 05:03.120
Isn't that a bit too loud, dude?

122
05:03.920 --> 05:06.720
[Dope, occupation: high school student]

123
05:07.140 --> 05:08.600
What's there to be afraid of?

124
05:08.600 --> 05:10.100
His father can handle this anyway.

125
05:10.210 --> 05:11.120
This way!

126
05:11.120 --> 05:11.750
Oh?

127
05:13.600 --> 05:16.360
[Dump, occupation: high school student]

128
05:16.590 --> 05:17.410
His father

129
05:17.430 --> 05:18.260
doesn't need yarn,

130
05:18.280 --> 05:19.320
thread,

131
05:19.390 --> 05:20.900
or rope!

132
05:23.420 --> 05:26.150
[Dape, occupation: high school student]

133
05:26.330 --> 05:29.040
Cause my father can pull the strings!

134
05:29.180 --> 05:30.720
If anyone in this dorm has an issue with us,

135
05:30.730 --> 05:32.620
just say my father's name.

136
05:33.690 --> 05:34.920
- Yeah. - Yeah.

137
05:36.040 --> 05:36.880
Surachet!

138
05:38.070 --> 05:39.070
Surachet!

139
05:40.170 --> 05:41.100
Surachet!

140
05:42.140 --> 05:43.020
Surachet!

141
05:43.760 --> 05:44.470
Ugh!

142
05:45.290 --> 05:46.010
Use it to threaten them,

143
05:46.010 --> 05:47.180
not to mock me!

144
05:51.060 --> 05:51.610
Hey.

145
05:57.220 --> 05:58.170
- Louder. - Do it louder.

146
05:59.880 --> 06:00.680
Call out to him.

147
06:00.680 --> 06:02.150
Hey!

148
06:03.200 --> 06:04.210
Ugh...

149
06:04.210 --> 06:05.560
Stop making loud noises.

150
06:05.560 --> 06:07.320
It's disturbing other tenants!

151
06:07.930 --> 06:09.620
Who told you about us?

152
06:10.040 --> 06:11.090
I did.

153
06:11.090 --> 06:12.040
- Wait. - Whoa.

154
06:13.340 --> 06:16.380
Am I so drunk that I'm seeing a bald softshell turtle?!

155
06:16.380 --> 06:17.320
Wow...

156
06:17.320 --> 06:18.210
I'm a kappa.

157
06:18.950 --> 06:19.560
Kappa...

158
06:19.560 --> 06:22.550
We were just celebrating after our exams.

159
06:22.710 --> 06:23.900
Hey,

160
06:24.350 --> 06:26.370
I understand you want to celebrate after your exams,

161
06:26.370 --> 06:27.620
but be more considerate.

162
06:27.660 --> 06:29.100
You're disturbing the others.

163
06:29.100 --> 06:29.750
Yeah.

164
06:29.750 --> 06:31.340
That's all I ask.

165
06:31.980 --> 06:33.270
If you asked...

166
06:34.040 --> 06:34.870
then I'll humor you!

167
06:36.020 --> 06:37.180
Without further ado,

168
06:37.180 --> 06:39.250
please enjoy the performance by

169
06:39.250 --> 06:41.450
Wat Nong Tao Ngoi School!

170
06:42.760 --> 06:43.659
Ugh, you...

171
06:43.659 --> 06:44.700
Every time you see a mic,

172
06:44.700 --> 06:45.560
you have to be an MC, huh?

173
06:45.560 --> 06:46.200
- Yeah. - What?

174
06:46.200 --> 06:47.120
It's muscle memory.

175
06:47.120 --> 06:47.730
Mm, understandable.

176
06:47.790 --> 06:48.450
Ugh...

177
06:48.770 --> 06:49.620
Guys,

178
06:49.620 --> 06:51.280
this is your first warning.

179
06:51.290 --> 06:52.850
Don't let there be a second time.

180
06:52.850 --> 06:53.980
What if there's a second time?

181
06:54.840 --> 06:55.840
There shouldn't be a third time.

182
06:55.840 --> 06:56.720
What about a fourth time?

183
06:56.720 --> 06:57.940
Don't let it happen a fourth time.

184
06:57.940 --> 06:58.800
Ugh!

185
06:58.980 --> 06:59.480
Hey,

186
06:59.480 --> 07:01.110
have you been beaten up by a kappa before?

187
07:02.180 --> 07:03.010
Kappa?

188
07:03.390 --> 07:05.320
- You want some?! - Whoa, whoa, whoa.

189
07:06.050 --> 07:06.950
Whoa, kiddos!

190
07:06.950 --> 07:09.060
Just high schoolers, yet so cocky.

191
07:09.200 --> 07:11.000
Why don't you tell your parents to come talk to me, hm?

192
07:11.010 --> 07:11.450
Yeah.

193
07:11.750 --> 07:12.990
Well, if my father came,

194
07:13.000 --> 07:15.390
will you be able to carry the consequences?

195
07:15.810 --> 07:16.960
Why would I need to carry anything?!

196
07:17.130 --> 07:18.810
Is your father diabetic and can't walk on his own?

197
07:18.810 --> 07:20.190
- Hey... - Whoa...

198
07:20.190 --> 07:21.640
Insulting my friend's father like this...

199
07:21.690 --> 07:23.280
- You want some?! - Whoa, whoa.

200
07:23.290 --> 07:24.480
- Chill. - He's fierce.

201
07:24.480 --> 07:26.520
He jumps headfirst into things, huh?

202
07:26.530 --> 07:28.390
Acting as if you were corn aphids.

203
07:28.390 --> 07:30.240
Since you came all the way here,

204
07:30.580 --> 07:32.840
let us sing you a cute song.

205
07:34.190 --> 07:35.790
Three, two, one...

206
07:35.810 --> 07:37.840
- ♫Goose kiss,♫ - ♫Starfish kiss,♫

207
07:37.880 --> 07:38.890
♫Goldfish kiss,♫

208
07:38.920 --> 07:39.980
♫Rooster kiss,♫

209
07:39.980 --> 07:42.990
♫Any kisses only for you♫

210
07:43.140 --> 07:43.680
Go.

211
07:43.680 --> 07:45.810
♫Kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss♫

212
07:45.810 --> 07:46.900
♫This kiss is for you♫

213
07:46.900 --> 07:47.340
Yeah.

214
07:47.340 --> 07:49.380
♫Kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss♫

215
07:49.380 --> 07:50.830
♫This heart is for you♫

216
07:50.830 --> 07:52.700
♫My heart, my heart, all for you♫

217
07:52.700 --> 07:54.020
♫This love is for no one else but you♫

218
07:54.020 --> 07:54.820
- Ugh! - ♫Kiss♫

219
07:54.820 --> 07:55.940
Go kiss your dad, then!

220
07:55.940 --> 07:56.400
Huh?!

221
07:57.200 --> 07:58.620
You should stop them!

222
07:58.820 --> 07:59.790
Why didn't you stop them?

223
07:59.790 --> 08:00.990
♫Kiss, kiss, kiss♫

224
08:00.990 --> 08:02.190
♫This kiss is for you♫

225
08:02.190 --> 08:04.100
♫Rooster kiss, starfish kiss,♫

226
08:04.100 --> 08:05.790
♫Goose kiss, kitty kiss,♫

227
08:05.820 --> 08:07.700
- Peek-a-boo... - Boo...

228
08:08.680 --> 08:09.400
Ugh!

229
08:10.080 --> 08:11.250
Hey...

230
08:11.250 --> 08:13.440
I think I'm fine with them

231
08:13.450 --> 08:15.040
singing this cute song

232
08:15.170 --> 08:16.280
from such a great agency.

233
08:16.590 --> 08:17.770
Mm, that's true...

234
08:17.940 --> 08:18.920
He's right.

235
08:19.330 --> 08:20.790
If you sing this song, it's fine.

236
08:20.820 --> 08:21.830
Mm.

237
08:21.860 --> 08:23.180
Just keep it down, alright?

238
08:23.440 --> 08:25.040
So, we can sing this song, right?

239
08:25.290 --> 08:26.190
Mm, I'm okay with that.

240
08:26.620 --> 08:27.160
Go.

241
08:27.160 --> 08:28.710
Alright, let's go.

242
08:28.920 --> 08:30.990
We'll keep it down, then.

243
08:30.990 --> 08:31.640
Mm.

244
08:39.450 --> 08:41.799
Are we really gonna play only cute songs, dude?

245
08:41.919 --> 08:43.090
Yeah, it's...

246
08:43.100 --> 08:45.250
We've become softies. We're so over.

247
08:50.620 --> 08:51.720
You got a plan?

248
08:54.080 --> 08:56.760
[The D Dorm]

249
08:58.170 --> 08:58.960
Mm...

250
08:59.280 --> 09:00.950
Mmm... Ooh...

251
09:03.350 --> 09:05.750
Mmm... Ooh...

252
09:10.550 --> 09:12.130
Mm...

253
09:14.070 --> 09:16.010
Gaysorn...

254
09:16.340 --> 09:17.800
I miss you.

255
09:19.130 --> 09:20.040
Ugh, Grandpa!

256
09:20.580 --> 09:21.660
What are you doing?!

257
09:21.660 --> 09:22.380
Disgusting!!

258
09:22.880 --> 09:23.750
What do you mean?

259
09:23.970 --> 09:24.360
Huh?

260
09:24.680 --> 09:25.540
What is disgusting?

261
09:25.540 --> 09:26.090
What?

262
09:26.370 --> 09:26.930
You were eating noodles?

263
09:27.400 --> 09:27.850
What?

264
09:28.010 --> 09:28.920
Why did you have to make that noise?

265
09:28.920 --> 09:30.350
Well, it is spicy!

266
09:30.690 --> 09:31.550
I don't mind the noise...

267
09:31.550 --> 09:32.560
but why did you move your hand like that?

268
09:32.600 --> 09:34.720
I am mixing the chili into the noodles.

269
09:34.840 --> 09:36.460
Why were you moaning Grandma Gaysorn's name?

270
09:36.460 --> 09:37.750
Well, this shop...

271
09:37.750 --> 09:38.890
has been open for a long time.

272
09:38.900 --> 09:40.690
I used to eat here with Gaysorn,

273
09:40.690 --> 09:42.940
so eating this again reminds me of her.

274
09:42.940 --> 09:44.150
Ugh...

275
09:44.850 --> 09:45.950
Can you eat quietly?

276
09:45.970 --> 09:48.180
Don't sit there calling Grandma Gaysorn's name like that.

277
09:50.150 --> 09:50.680
Hey.

278
09:50.970 --> 09:52.070
- Mmm... - Whoa.

279
09:52.070 --> 09:52.890
Ooh...

280
09:52.890 --> 09:54.400
Stop making that noise.

281
09:54.550 --> 09:55.740
Eat quietly, Grandpa.

282
09:56.370 --> 09:57.060
Wait.

283
09:57.350 --> 09:58.040
Why...

284
09:58.230 --> 09:59.430
is there so much food?

285
09:59.430 --> 10:00.290
Don't tell me...

286
10:00.410 --> 10:01.560
you stole from a three-way crossroads?

287
10:02.740 --> 10:03.350
Hey,

288
10:03.650 --> 10:05.570
I am not a wandering spirit.

289
10:05.570 --> 10:06.950
I have a place to dwell!

290
10:06.950 --> 10:07.830
Well, you seem like one.

291
10:08.910 --> 10:10.440
I do not know either.

292
10:10.440 --> 10:12.250
Perhaps someone gave me their offerings.

293
10:12.680 --> 10:13.410
Who, though?

294
10:13.780 --> 10:14.520
Danis?

295
10:14.520 --> 10:15.520
I do not think so.

296
10:16.050 --> 10:16.700
Mom?

297
10:16.970 --> 10:18.240
Mm...maybe?

298
10:18.240 --> 10:19.060
I don't think so,

299
10:19.060 --> 10:19.820
she hates your guts.

300
10:20.290 --> 10:20.810
Wait...

301
10:20.980 --> 10:21.570
maybe it was me.

302
10:21.570 --> 10:23.100
Oh, thank you so much, my beloved grandson.

303
10:23.110 --> 10:24.610
It's such a waste of my time, though.

304
10:24.620 --> 10:25.640
Wow, you ungrateful grandson.

305
10:26.640 --> 10:27.660
Who is it, then, Grandpa?

306
10:28.990 --> 10:30.020
Where did Thai music come from?

307
10:30.970 --> 10:31.610
Hey,

308
10:31.860 --> 10:32.640
do you hear that?

309
10:32.640 --> 10:34.050
Who is playing ranat in the morning?

310
10:35.130 --> 10:35.720
Hey...

311
10:36.360 --> 10:36.950
Wait.

312
10:37.700 --> 10:38.660
- Whoa... - It's loud.

313
10:38.660 --> 10:39.700
What is happening?

314
10:40.330 --> 10:41.440
- Huh? - Grandpa?

315
10:41.570 --> 10:42.170
What's wrong?

316
10:42.360 --> 10:42.950
I do not know...

317
10:42.990 --> 10:43.440
Whoa!

318
10:43.440 --> 10:43.930
Hey!

319
10:44.470 --> 10:45.160
Grandpa?

320
10:45.350 --> 10:46.210
What's wrong?

321
10:46.860 --> 10:48.300
I do not know either!

322
10:50.320 --> 10:52.120
- Dobby, help me! - Whoa!

323
10:52.250 --> 10:53.750
Dobby, help me!

324
10:53.750 --> 10:56.700
- Dobby! - Grandpa!

325
10:57.110 --> 10:58.120
Grandpa!

326
10:58.210 --> 10:58.690
Oh, crap!

327
10:58.690 --> 10:59.830
What happened, Grandpa?!

328
11:12.010 --> 11:12.840
What even is this?

329
11:13.800 --> 11:16.320
Dobby, please help me.

330
11:16.320 --> 11:18.370
I do not want to watch this ritual dance.

331
11:18.370 --> 11:20.090
I was forced to be here!

332
11:22.720 --> 11:23.380
Hey...

333
11:23.380 --> 11:24.010
Hm?

334
11:24.010 --> 11:25.930
Why is Auntie Duang suddenly dancing here?

335
11:25.930 --> 11:27.710
What's with all these offerings?

336
11:28.000 --> 11:29.750
Auntie Duang had a dream

337
11:29.750 --> 11:31.050
that Gramps came to tell her lottery numbers.

338
11:31.290 --> 11:33.350
The tenants bought it, and many won.

339
11:33.350 --> 11:35.440
That's why they all came to worship Gramps.

340
11:36.520 --> 11:38.820
I have never told anyone anything.

341
11:38.820 --> 11:40.380
They came up with that on their own!

342
11:40.380 --> 11:42.760
You know I do not know how to get into people's dreams.

343
11:43.370 --> 11:44.150
Yeah...

344
11:44.280 --> 11:44.940
- Daeng. - Hm?

345
11:44.960 --> 11:45.810
Look at Auntie Duang.

346
11:46.040 --> 11:47.830
She met Gramps, and he gave her the numbers.

347
11:48.010 --> 11:49.060
What about you?

348
11:49.320 --> 11:51.250
Why didn't you and Dawin get anything?

349
11:51.250 --> 11:52.140
You're no good.

350
11:52.380 --> 11:52.930
Hm?

351
11:53.100 --> 11:53.750
Hey...

352
11:54.240 --> 11:55.180
Sadhu, Gramps,

353
11:55.490 --> 11:57.140
if you let me win the lottery,

354
11:57.170 --> 11:58.360
I won't keep a single baht.

355
11:58.360 --> 11:59.400
I'll give it all to the tenants.

356
11:59.400 --> 12:00.750
- Not you too... - Won't you regret that?

357
12:00.800 --> 12:01.860
Why would I? It's not gonna happen anyway.

358
12:01.860 --> 12:02.340
What?

359
12:02.340 --> 12:03.350
Oh, not you too.

360
12:03.480 --> 12:04.100
Gramps,

361
12:04.100 --> 12:05.070
to keep it simple, for this draw,

362
12:05.070 --> 12:06.750
give me three of those.

363
12:06.950 --> 12:07.700
Puppies?

364
12:07.720 --> 12:08.360
Nails.

365
12:09.000 --> 12:09.860
We've been together for so long,

366
12:09.870 --> 12:10.960
yet our jokes never clicked.

367
12:10.960 --> 12:12.080
I don't want the numbers anymore.

368
12:12.080 --> 12:13.280
Go break his neck instead.

369
12:13.280 --> 12:13.800
Hey!

370
12:13.800 --> 12:14.510
I'll break your neck.

371
12:14.510 --> 12:15.400
I'm older than you!

372
12:15.570 --> 12:16.010
Don't...

373
12:16.550 --> 12:17.330
Gramps...

374
12:17.750 --> 12:19.540
- Ugh... - They fight, as expected.

375
12:21.200 --> 12:24.040
I danced just like you asked, Gramps.

376
12:24.780 --> 12:28.210
If you give me a big win in this lottery draw,

377
12:28.210 --> 12:29.680
I'll put on a big show for you.

378
12:29.750 --> 12:32.150
Whether it's Thai traditional dance,

379
12:32.500 --> 12:35.220
Chinese traditional dance,

380
12:35.360 --> 12:36.270
or...

381
12:37.290 --> 12:38.360
Indonesian traditional dance,

382
12:41.100 --> 12:41.750
or even

383
12:42.010 --> 12:43.380
twerking!

384
12:43.380 --> 12:44.480
Twerking!

385
12:44.480 --> 12:45.620
Twerking!

386
12:45.620 --> 12:46.440
So annoying!!

387
12:46.440 --> 12:47.940
I'm gonna give you the full show!

388
12:47.940 --> 12:48.810
No need!

389
12:48.810 --> 12:50.400
I do not want any of that!

390
12:53.900 --> 12:54.560
Gramps,

391
12:54.770 --> 12:55.430
how about this?

392
12:55.430 --> 12:56.470
If I won the first prize in the lottery...

393
12:56.470 --> 12:57.770
Forget this little show.

394
12:57.770 --> 12:59.150
I'd hire Rabiab Wathasilp

395
12:59.160 --> 13:00.410
for seven days and seven nights.

396
13:00.950 --> 13:01.580
Ugh...

397
13:01.580 --> 13:03.280
Guard Dum, please don't go that far.

398
13:03.350 --> 13:04.740
The tenants have already complained

399
13:04.850 --> 13:07.360
about these offerings.

400
13:07.520 --> 13:09.490
And there are also those kids in Room 310.

401
13:09.490 --> 13:11.010
- Yeah. - God...they're loud.

402
13:11.020 --> 13:12.600
I'm getting a lot of complaints.

403
13:12.920 --> 13:14.880
Come on, Danis,

404
13:14.880 --> 13:16.550
I'm only asking for a small space.

405
13:16.550 --> 13:17.590
I promise

406
13:17.600 --> 13:19.260
I won't cause any trouble,

407
13:19.260 --> 13:20.770
unlike those kids in Room 310.

408
13:21.480 --> 13:24.440
Prime Minister Noo gave us 60/40.

409
13:24.810 --> 13:26.900
But Gramps can give us a hundred times more here.

410
13:26.900 --> 13:28.550
I guarantee the economy will prosper!

411
13:28.550 --> 13:29.360
Ugh...

412
13:29.360 --> 13:30.250
That is even worse.

413
13:30.250 --> 13:31.640
- What economy, Auntie? - Right?

414
13:32.000 --> 13:32.970
You'll know soon enough.

415
13:33.490 --> 13:34.420
Oh, that doesn't sound good.

416
13:36.130 --> 13:37.680
Sadhu, sadhu.

417
13:39.320 --> 13:41.470
[The D Dorm]

418
13:41.640 --> 13:42.410
Come this way. [Gramps' Vow Offerings]

419
13:42.410 --> 13:43.660
One hundred and ninety-nine times two.

420
13:43.660 --> 13:44.430
Your change.

421
13:44.430 --> 13:45.620
Thanks...

422
13:45.860 --> 13:47.640
Sadhu, sadhu.

423
13:48.210 --> 13:49.790
Wow...

424
13:49.850 --> 13:52.330
This is only going to make your economy prosper, isn't it?

425
13:53.620 --> 13:56.050
Well, have some empathy for me.

426
13:56.070 --> 13:57.860
I'm a single mom with two kids,

427
13:57.880 --> 13:59.180
and I'm getting old.

428
13:59.180 --> 14:01.610
My boys are still growing up, too.

429
14:04.800 --> 14:05.300
Mm...

430
14:07.400 --> 14:08.600
- Oh... - Oh, wow...

431
14:08.680 --> 14:09.780
Whoa...

432
14:11.000 --> 14:12.370
- Hey. - Ooh...

433
14:12.910 --> 14:13.900
What are you doing?

434
14:14.410 --> 14:14.900
Huh?

435
14:15.350 --> 14:17.130
I want to drink bubble tea, but I feel guilty,

436
14:17.400 --> 14:18.360
so I do it while working out.

437
14:18.640 --> 14:19.410
See?

438
14:19.410 --> 14:20.520
A real gym rat spotted...

439
14:22.280 --> 14:22.780
By the way, Mom?

440
14:22.780 --> 14:23.280
Hm?

441
14:23.280 --> 14:24.950
Have you talked to Danis

442
14:25.170 --> 14:26.530
about building a shrine for Gramps?

443
14:26.530 --> 14:27.560
- Hm? - Huh?

444
14:27.760 --> 14:28.570
What shrine?

445
14:32.920 --> 14:34.820
I was just planning ahead

446
14:34.900 --> 14:37.350
in case Gramps becomes popular.

447
14:37.350 --> 14:39.350
We can build a shrine to get lots of people to come worship him.

448
14:39.350 --> 14:41.170
People will rent rooms in the dorm,

449
14:41.170 --> 14:43.200
and my business will boom.

450
14:43.200 --> 14:44.470
Then everyone

451
14:44.470 --> 14:45.750
will be complaining,

452
14:45.770 --> 14:47.230
"I'm so rich, I can't take it anymore!"

453
14:47.250 --> 14:48.420
Whoa...

454
14:48.420 --> 14:50.050
I can't, I can't, I can't...

455
14:50.980 --> 14:52.550
I can't see that working out, Auntie.

456
14:53.420 --> 14:55.760
If people know this dorm is haunted, who's gonna purchase it?

457
14:56.020 --> 14:56.610
Purchase?

458
14:58.550 --> 14:59.200
Purchase what?

459
14:59.630 --> 15:01.560
Didn't you say you weren't going to sell this dorm anymore?

460
15:09.200 --> 15:10.160
You misheard me.

461
15:10.550 --> 15:11.920
I... I mean "hire purchase."

462
15:12.520 --> 15:13.460
Think about it.

463
15:13.460 --> 15:15.010
If people know this dorm is haunted,

464
15:15.350 --> 15:16.610
will they want to live here?

465
15:16.660 --> 15:18.010
No one would dare rent a room here.

466
15:18.160 --> 15:20.510
Not everyone's crazy about the lottery like you, Auntie.

467
15:24.660 --> 15:26.620
Please don't go that far, Auntie.

468
15:26.620 --> 15:28.570
It'll disturb the other tenants.

469
15:29.090 --> 15:29.750
That's right, Auntie.

470
15:30.410 --> 15:30.950
Right?

471
15:31.780 --> 15:32.360
Yeah...

472
15:33.350 --> 15:33.920
Oh!

473
15:42.120 --> 15:43.060
Stay still.

474
15:46.680 --> 15:47.540
Hold on to this, Dum.

475
15:47.570 --> 15:48.150
Okay.

476
15:48.170 --> 15:49.040
Uh, Mr. Drip?

477
15:49.490 --> 15:50.360
Can you please grab...

478
15:50.370 --> 15:51.510
that screwdriver for me?

479
15:51.520 --> 15:52.580
Of course, Handyman.

480
15:53.090 --> 15:54.220
♫Wh...who said I'm shivering?♫

481
15:54.220 --> 15:54.950
Oh, crap!

482
15:55.740 --> 15:56.440
[DO-MUN-DRIP]

483
15:56.450 --> 15:57.170
Whoa...

484
15:59.050 --> 16:00.360
How captivating!

485
16:00.740 --> 16:02.150
This is art.

486
16:31.760 --> 16:32.440
What even is that?

487
16:35.970 --> 16:37.000
Can I hold your hand?

488
16:37.040 --> 16:38.230
- Ugh! - Let me hold your hand.

489
16:38.290 --> 16:38.860
Let go!

490
16:38.880 --> 16:40.080
Don't touch me! Let go!

491
16:40.260 --> 16:40.900
What are you doing?

492
16:41.140 --> 16:41.750
I see...

493
16:41.750 --> 16:43.250
Double double this this,

494
16:43.250 --> 16:44.760
double double that that,

495
16:44.760 --> 16:46.140
double this, double that,

496
16:46.140 --> 16:47.580
double double this that.

497
16:47.580 --> 16:48.350
- Hey! - Ugh!

498
16:50.210 --> 16:51.120
Hey...

499
16:51.270 --> 16:53.120
you're still trying to hold Daeng the Handyman's hand, Dawin?

500
16:54.380 --> 16:56.150
I don't think holding hands

501
16:56.350 --> 16:58.440
has anything to do with you seeing Gramps' ghost the other day.

502
16:58.550 --> 16:59.690
It doesn't.

503
16:59.960 --> 17:02.200
My brother and I have been holding hands since we were kids,

504
17:02.330 --> 17:03.720
but I've never seen a ghost before.

505
17:03.720 --> 17:04.819
Look.

506
17:06.950 --> 17:07.859
What...?

507
17:08.880 --> 17:09.630
Can you see ghosts, Guard Dum?

508
17:10.089 --> 17:10.730
I'm getting electrocuted...

509
17:10.730 --> 17:11.349
- Whoa? - Let go.

510
17:11.569 --> 17:12.599
I'll kick you off!

511
17:12.619 --> 17:13.480
Daeng... You...

512
17:13.640 --> 17:14.970
Ugh, I can't let go of this either.

513
17:18.140 --> 17:18.960
Ugh!

514
17:24.630 --> 17:25.859
I was wondering...

515
17:25.940 --> 17:27.869
If we held hands,

516
17:28.260 --> 17:29.220
would we see any ghosts?

517
17:35.730 --> 17:37.400
I don't see any "ghosts"

518
17:38.820 --> 17:40.100
Only a "good" eye candy

519
17:41.040 --> 17:41.620
Huh?

520
17:43.140 --> 17:43.620
Uh...

521
17:44.150 --> 17:45.210
Oops... I'm sorry.

522
17:45.610 --> 17:46.210
Um...

523
17:46.840 --> 17:47.750
Dawin!

524
17:47.750 --> 17:49.270
Why would you want to see Gramps' ghost again?

525
17:49.470 --> 17:51.360
Do you want to ask for lottery numbers...like Mom did?

526
17:53.010 --> 17:53.750
Well...

527
17:54.340 --> 17:56.180
I just want to prove

528
17:56.580 --> 17:58.120
if I have the ability to see ghosts.

529
18:01.080 --> 18:02.090
If you want to see ghosts,

530
18:02.100 --> 18:04.420
there are many other ways apart from holding my brother's hand.

531
18:04.730 --> 18:05.560
To keep it simple,

532
18:05.560 --> 18:06.880
you can look between your legs.

533
18:07.940 --> 18:09.000
- Ow! - Ow...

534
18:09.020 --> 18:09.540
Whoa...

535
18:09.540 --> 18:11.750
Come on, Daeng...

536
18:12.170 --> 18:13.700
I tried a lot of methods

537
18:14.050 --> 18:15.060
ever since I was little,

538
18:15.220 --> 18:16.370
but nothing worked.

539
18:16.750 --> 18:17.750
What?

540
18:18.060 --> 18:18.950
Have you always...

541
18:18.950 --> 18:21.060
wanted to see ghosts ever since you were young?

542
18:21.600 --> 18:22.120
Why?

543
18:24.120 --> 18:25.440
I just want to see them.

544
18:25.650 --> 18:26.980
Why are you asking so many questions?

545
18:28.880 --> 18:30.120
I tried everything.

546
18:30.580 --> 18:31.840
From looking between my legs,

547
18:32.610 --> 18:33.730
wearing dead people's clothes,

548
18:34.570 --> 18:36.180
and I even applied the dirt from seven cemeteries to my eyes.

549
18:37.060 --> 18:37.850
Oh.

550
18:38.340 --> 18:40.000
But there's one method I haven't tried yet.

551
18:40.140 --> 18:41.250
That is using a black dog's tear.

552
18:42.710 --> 18:43.210
What?

553
18:43.690 --> 18:44.860
Why didn't you try it?

554
18:45.020 --> 18:47.120
I don't know how to make a dog cry.

555
18:47.600 --> 18:48.750
I've hit a dog with a stick before,

556
18:49.200 --> 18:50.450
but it bit me...

557
18:50.770 --> 18:52.340
So I ended up crying instead...

558
18:52.620 --> 18:53.750
- Whoa. - Ugh...

559
18:54.080 --> 18:55.090
Serves you right!

560
18:55.090 --> 18:56.330
You were asking for trouble

561
18:56.330 --> 18:57.260
trying to see ghosts like that.

562
18:59.430 --> 19:00.470
Would you like to try it out tonight?

563
19:01.530 --> 19:02.360
If you want to,

564
19:02.370 --> 19:04.350
I'll take you to get a black dog's tear.

565
19:06.920 --> 19:07.930
I want to go, too, Guard!

566
19:08.560 --> 19:09.570
I've never seen

567
19:09.890 --> 19:11.380
a ghost before in my life.

568
19:11.600 --> 19:13.310
You're talking about ghosts here, not Justin Bieber.

569
19:13.570 --> 19:14.860
Why would you want to see ghosts anyway?

570
19:15.020 --> 19:16.200
You all can go if you want,

571
19:16.350 --> 19:17.360
but leave me out of this.

572
19:17.780 --> 19:18.950
Then...

573
19:18.960 --> 19:20.130
who would like to join me tonight?

574
19:20.140 --> 19:20.710
- Hey! - Me!

575
19:21.440 --> 19:22.140
Ah...

576
19:22.140 --> 19:23.210
Everyone wants to go.

577
19:23.420 --> 19:24.370
You'll have to be alone tonight.

578
19:25.820 --> 19:26.830
- I'll go, too. - Huh?

579
19:28.280 --> 19:30.350
[The D Dorm]

580
19:39.170 --> 19:42.790
Since when did my room become a house of a softshell turtle?

581
19:44.860 --> 19:45.810
Grandpa, I feel bad for him.

582
19:45.820 --> 19:46.610
Let him rest.

583
19:47.590 --> 19:49.240
He was filming a series late into the night,

584
19:49.390 --> 19:51.300
and he had to wake up to the set again in the morning.

585
19:52.390 --> 19:53.400
Just let him get some sleep.

586
19:55.200 --> 19:56.150
Back then,

587
19:56.930 --> 19:57.930
your mother...

588
19:58.550 --> 20:00.950
asked me if she could have a pet turtle.

589
20:01.860 --> 20:03.350
But I did not allow her that,

590
20:04.550 --> 20:06.920
because turtle cages stink.

591
20:07.910 --> 20:08.920
Then your mother...

592
20:09.610 --> 20:10.980
tried to act cute

593
20:11.900 --> 20:12.910
by singing:

594
20:13.390 --> 20:15.730
♫Turtles have four legs♫

595
20:15.750 --> 20:18.200
♫Four feet marching our way♫

596
20:18.200 --> 20:20.810
♫Showing and hiding its head♫

597
20:22.530 --> 20:23.460
When she was little...

598
20:24.120 --> 20:25.330
she was adorable.

599
20:26.520 --> 20:27.920
But once she grew up...

600
20:28.960 --> 20:29.460
So stubborn.

601
20:30.400 --> 20:32.120
I wanted to shove ashes into her mouth.

602
20:33.150 --> 20:34.860
Well, Grandpa,

603
20:34.880 --> 20:36.190
if I were Mom,

604
20:36.760 --> 20:37.690
I'd chew those ashes.

605
20:37.690 --> 20:39.040
Chew, chew, chew, chew...

606
20:39.040 --> 20:40.330
And spit them right in your face.

607
20:41.960 --> 20:42.720
Hey, Grandpa,

608
20:42.720 --> 20:43.890
just admit it already that

609
20:43.900 --> 20:45.970
these days, my mom lives a happy life.

610
20:46.030 --> 20:47.220
She owns a house

611
20:47.510 --> 20:48.560
and a restaurant.

612
20:49.140 --> 20:50.730
She has a great husband.

613
20:51.040 --> 20:52.180
And most importantly,

614
20:53.310 --> 20:54.250
she has a son who is...

615
20:54.270 --> 20:55.190
so freaking handsome.

616
20:55.930 --> 20:57.440
"So freaking irritating" is more accurate.

617
20:58.550 --> 20:59.660
Back then...

618
21:00.020 --> 21:01.950
- What? - If your mother had listened to me

619
21:01.950 --> 21:04.100
and married the person I chose for her...

620
21:04.100 --> 21:05.190
Yeah? What would happen?

621
21:05.190 --> 21:06.780
Her life

622
21:07.120 --> 21:09.480
might have been better than this.

623
21:09.660 --> 21:11.670
She would not be drowning in debts.

624
21:11.750 --> 21:14.000
She would have had a rich

625
21:14.070 --> 21:15.750
and nice husband

626
21:16.010 --> 21:19.580
who provides for his family and makes them happy.

627
21:21.070 --> 21:23.140
And when her kid grew up...

628
21:23.230 --> 21:24.440
they would've been a sweet child,

629
21:25.280 --> 21:26.800
not an irritating one like you are.

630
21:28.080 --> 21:28.760
Hey,

631
21:28.760 --> 21:30.400
it's passed down through our genes, alright?

632
21:30.760 --> 21:32.400
I'm irritating just like you are, Grandpa.

633
21:33.730 --> 21:34.550
Are you insulting me?!

634
21:35.750 --> 21:36.950
Well, there are only the two of us here.

635
21:36.950 --> 21:37.680
Who else would I be insulting?

636
21:37.690 --> 21:39.560
I thought you were insulting that softshell turtle.

637
21:39.930 --> 21:40.890
Whoa...

638
21:41.860 --> 21:42.950
Little Tangkwa...

639
21:43.410 --> 21:44.440
Tangkwa...

640
21:44.450 --> 21:45.240
Oh, he's talking in his sleep.

641
21:45.490 --> 21:46.360
Who is Tangkwa?

642
21:46.360 --> 21:47.160
I don't know either.

643
21:48.960 --> 21:50.570
- Whoa. That's loud. - ♫Starfish kiss♫

644
21:50.580 --> 21:51.590
♫Starfish kiss♫

645
21:51.600 --> 21:52.660
They're doing it at night, too.

646
21:52.670 --> 21:54.460
♫Kitty kiss♫

647
21:54.470 --> 21:56.100
♫Starfish kiss♫

648
21:56.110 --> 21:58.110
♫Starfish kiss♫

649
21:59.680 --> 22:01.300
♫Goldfish kiss♫

650
22:01.310 --> 22:03.470
♫All kisses for you♫

651
22:10.100 --> 22:11.300
This room again?

652
22:11.490 --> 22:12.600
They're even louder than the last time.

653
22:12.600 --> 22:13.940
No matter how many times I knocked, they wouldn't open.

654
22:14.520 --> 22:15.410
Danis, move.

655
22:15.620 --> 22:16.000
Whoa.

656
22:16.000 --> 22:17.120
- Huh? - I'll break the door down.

657
22:17.480 --> 22:17.960
Huh?!

658
22:18.080 --> 22:18.950
Three...

659
22:19.430 --> 22:20.220
Two...

660
22:20.490 --> 22:21.050
One.

661
22:22.410 --> 22:23.240
- Whoa! - Whoa!

662
22:23.940 --> 22:25.370
Hey, are you alright?

663
22:25.530 --> 22:25.940
Hey!

664
22:27.150 --> 22:29.460
Am I really seeing a police officer slipping and sliding

665
22:29.480 --> 22:31.380
over there...?

666
22:33.800 --> 22:34.550
Get up.

667
22:34.550 --> 22:35.040
Are you okay?

668
22:35.040 --> 22:36.050
I'm fine.

669
22:36.060 --> 22:36.630
Hey...

670
22:37.240 --> 22:38.320
You opened the door without warning.

671
22:40.240 --> 22:41.400
Hey,

672
22:41.610 --> 22:43.300
didn't you say you'd keep it down?

673
22:43.660 --> 22:44.830
You said you'd sing cute songs.

674
22:44.960 --> 22:45.720
Yeah.

675
22:45.730 --> 22:46.890
This is the same song.

676
22:47.080 --> 22:48.570
The "JuBu Jub" song we told you.

677
22:48.760 --> 22:50.040
It's just a bit more hardcore.

678
22:50.050 --> 22:50.660
How?

679
22:50.940 --> 22:52.980
♫Goose kiss♫

680
22:52.980 --> 22:54.700
♫Starfish kiss♫

681
22:54.700 --> 22:56.480
- ♫Goldfish kiss♫ - Hey!

682
22:56.480 --> 22:57.050
Hey!

683
22:57.050 --> 22:58.300
♫Rooster kiss♫

684
22:58.300 --> 23:02.730
♫All kisses for you♫

685
23:03.020 --> 23:03.920
Ugh!

686
23:04.120 --> 23:05.020
Be quiet!!

687
23:06.600 --> 23:07.790
I told you to stop them,

688
23:08.150 --> 23:09.410
but you played along again!

689
23:10.680 --> 23:11.600
Stop! I said stop!

690
23:12.060 --> 23:12.720
How could I stop?

691
23:12.720 --> 23:13.980
He's still stepping on my foot.

692
23:13.980 --> 23:14.900
Oh... Oops.

693
23:15.480 --> 23:16.320
Ugh...

694
23:16.330 --> 23:19.600
I was about to hear them say, "Giraffe kiss."

695
23:21.800 --> 23:22.550
Hey,

696
23:23.100 --> 23:24.760
you won't listen when I talk to you nicely,

697
23:24.760 --> 23:25.400
huh?

698
23:28.380 --> 23:29.370
What about it?

699
23:34.300 --> 23:35.560
You're all grown ass high schoolers.

700
23:35.560 --> 23:36.950
Learn some manners, won't you?

701
23:36.950 --> 23:37.830
Ooh...

702
23:37.960 --> 23:39.850
This is a shared space, not a private one.

703
23:39.850 --> 23:41.520
Learn to think of others.

704
23:41.520 --> 23:43.150
Don't be so selfish. Do you understand?

705
23:43.150 --> 23:44.320
But we...

706
23:44.320 --> 23:45.040
Shut up!

707
23:45.040 --> 23:46.170
The adult is talking. Do not interrupt me.

708
23:46.170 --> 23:47.710
Didn't anyone teach you this?

709
23:47.720 --> 23:48.950
Didn't your parents teach you manners?

710
23:48.950 --> 23:50.410
I'll teach you myself, then.

711
23:50.410 --> 23:52.000
Think of your parents when you do things.

712
23:52.000 --> 23:53.750
Then when people insult you, your parents won't be dragged into it.

713
23:53.750 --> 23:55.300
They sent you here to study, not to act like assholes.

714
23:55.300 --> 23:55.920
Do you understand?

715
23:56.850 --> 23:58.840
Who do you think you are to lecture us?

716
23:58.850 --> 23:59.570
That's right!

717
23:59.580 --> 24:00.490
Didn't your school teach you?!

718
24:00.490 --> 24:01.570
This is a dorm.

719
24:01.690 --> 24:03.090
If you can't keep it down,

720
24:03.100 --> 24:04.780
then go live at home!

721
24:04.890 --> 24:06.170
Dobby, why are you quiet?

722
24:06.170 --> 24:07.370
Help me out. Say something, will you?

723
24:07.370 --> 24:08.540
Dobby, can you hear me?!

724
24:08.540 --> 24:09.100
Ugh...

725
24:09.100 --> 24:11.230
You've said it all. I don't need to say anything anymore.

726
24:11.610 --> 24:12.950
Scolding them is a waste of time.

727
24:13.340 --> 24:14.710
Just kick all three of them out!

728
24:14.730 --> 24:15.620
- Yeah! - What?

729
24:15.620 --> 24:16.850
You can't do that.

730
24:16.980 --> 24:17.750
You want problems, huh?!

731
24:17.760 --> 24:19.400
- Whoa! - Hey... Calm down, Dump.

732
24:20.640 --> 24:22.000
There's a reason

733
24:22.010 --> 24:22.890
we were so loud.

734
24:22.900 --> 24:23.730
What is it?

735
24:24.710 --> 24:25.970
We...

736
24:26.850 --> 24:27.850
We were scared...

737
24:29.750 --> 24:30.480
Scared of what?

738
24:32.180 --> 24:33.120
We were scared of Gramps' ghost!

739
24:33.460 --> 24:34.380
- Whoa! - Huh?!

740
24:37.990 --> 24:39.000
Not me...

741
24:39.220 --> 24:39.730
What?

742
24:40.050 --> 24:41.000
Well, Gramps' ghost

743
24:41.000 --> 24:42.750
haunted us in our dreams.

744
24:42.750 --> 24:43.380
True.

745
24:46.010 --> 24:46.830
No, I did not!

746
24:47.010 --> 24:48.950
When did I even do that?

747
24:49.180 --> 24:50.890
That was not me. I did not do it!

748
24:52.200 --> 24:53.680
Don't use Gramps' ghost as an excuse.

749
24:53.920 --> 24:54.730
Why not?

750
24:55.100 --> 24:55.940
Gramps even...

751
24:55.950 --> 24:57.780
visited your mom in her dreams and told her about the lottery.

752
24:58.080 --> 24:59.600
So why couldn't he haunt us in our dreams, too?

753
24:59.620 --> 25:00.240
That's right!

754
25:00.560 --> 25:02.460
See, he haunts us every night. We couldn't sleep.

755
25:02.550 --> 25:04.000
We're the victims here,

756
25:04.100 --> 25:05.770
so how can you kick us out?!

757
25:06.060 --> 25:08.540
- Yeah. - Be grateful we haven't told our parents.

758
25:08.590 --> 25:09.540
- Get out! Go! - Yeah!

759
25:09.540 --> 25:09.940
Leave.

760
25:09.950 --> 25:11.170
- Go, go, go. - Guys, calm down.

761
25:11.180 --> 25:13.000
- Shouldn't a police officer be catching criminals? - Get out already.

762
25:13.010 --> 25:14.410
- Leave us. - Go away.

763
25:14.420 --> 25:15.350
- Get out of here. - Hey...

764
25:15.350 --> 25:16.550
- Don't use Grandpa's ghost as an excuse! - Let's talk.

765
25:16.550 --> 25:18.550
- Get out! Leave! - Don't push me, hey!

766
25:18.660 --> 25:19.240
Hey.

767
25:19.530 --> 25:20.730
These kids!

768
25:20.730 --> 25:21.920
I even brought a police officer with me,

769
25:21.920 --> 25:23.520
but it didn't seem to help at all.

770
25:23.520 --> 25:24.820
Well... Even if I arrested them,

771
25:24.820 --> 25:26.490
the police could only fine and give them a warning.

772
25:26.500 --> 25:27.840
They'd just be allowed to go home.

773
25:29.100 --> 25:29.890
I don't think fining them

774
25:29.900 --> 25:31.210
is enough to make them learn a lesson.

775
25:31.500 --> 25:33.320
They used Grandpa's ghost as an excuse, huh?

776
25:34.780 --> 25:35.750
Fine!

777
25:35.750 --> 25:37.400
We'll see about this!

778
25:45.130 --> 25:46.010
So scary...

779
25:56.150 --> 25:57.220
Hey... What?

780
25:58.060 --> 25:59.750
Everyone, keep it down.

781
26:00.660 --> 26:01.460
Under this cardboard box,

782
26:01.460 --> 26:03.640
there is a black dog with newborn pups.

783
26:04.360 --> 26:06.020
I'm still wondering

784
26:06.130 --> 26:07.420
how to get her tears?

785
26:08.960 --> 26:10.680
Maybe put on a sad episode from 'Love Upon a Time'?

786
26:11.750 --> 26:12.950
If you're just going to be annoying,

787
26:13.070 --> 26:13.860
then keep quiet.

788
26:13.870 --> 26:14.780
Stop talking.

789
26:15.460 --> 26:16.550
Be serious.

790
26:17.290 --> 26:18.720
Getting her tears is easy.

791
26:19.340 --> 26:20.760
We only have to take one of her pups.

792
26:21.170 --> 26:22.720
And when the pup wakes up and doesn't see its mother,

793
26:22.730 --> 26:23.920
it will cry out,

794
26:23.920 --> 26:24.950
"Mama!"

795
26:25.110 --> 26:26.120
We'll get the tears that way.

796
26:26.360 --> 26:28.040
- Whoa... - Yeah!

797
26:28.240 --> 26:29.040
Hey,

798
26:29.040 --> 26:30.990
you're evil to the core, Guard Dum.

799
26:31.330 --> 26:32.440
I'll take that as a compliment.

800
26:38.150 --> 26:38.740
Whoa...

801
26:40.440 --> 26:41.750
From the direction of her tail,

802
26:41.960 --> 26:43.580
she's probably facing that way.

803
26:44.400 --> 26:46.160
And her pups are probably cuddling over here.

804
26:46.820 --> 26:49.780
I want one brave volunteer

805
26:50.580 --> 26:51.600
who will take one of the pups out.

806
26:51.750 --> 26:53.460
If you volunteer, please step forward.

807
26:56.280 --> 26:56.820
Wow...

808
26:56.820 --> 26:57.910
You're very brave, Mr. Drip.

809
26:59.540 --> 27:00.140
What?!

810
27:00.140 --> 27:00.770
Whoa!

811
27:01.900 --> 27:02.910
I didn't volunteer,

812
27:02.910 --> 27:04.030
and I didn't step forward.

813
27:04.330 --> 27:05.180
It's alright.

814
27:05.300 --> 27:06.400
If I could do it, I would.

815
27:06.410 --> 27:08.280
But I couldn't bend over because of my belly.

816
27:08.640 --> 27:09.600
Come on... This way.

817
27:09.800 --> 27:10.550
You're amazing.

818
27:10.550 --> 27:11.460
I'm impressed.

819
27:11.580 --> 27:12.540
Go on. She's right there.

820
27:12.540 --> 27:13.820
Go ahead, Mr. Drip.

821
27:13.820 --> 27:14.890
It's not scary.

822
27:17.260 --> 27:18.210
Go on. Over there.

823
27:18.650 --> 27:20.150
Do you really think I'm brave enough for this?

824
27:20.170 --> 27:21.020
It's going to be fine.

825
27:33.600 --> 27:34.290
Found it.

826
27:34.520 --> 27:35.490
- Whoa! - Wow...

827
27:35.700 --> 27:36.620
The dog's hair is pretty long.

828
27:36.620 --> 27:37.920
I think this is a poodle.

829
27:38.150 --> 27:38.850
Yeah...

830
27:38.850 --> 27:39.770
This breed is friendly.

831
27:41.870 --> 27:43.220
It's balding here.

832
27:44.020 --> 27:45.350
Probably scabies.

833
27:46.550 --> 27:47.750
Poor thing...

834
27:50.800 --> 27:52.250
There's something long here.

835
27:54.230 --> 27:55.300
This one might be a male pup.

836
27:55.840 --> 27:57.960
- Oh... - I see...

837
27:58.490 --> 27:59.330
And...

838
28:01.330 --> 28:02.330
Seems like there's a hole, too.

839
28:02.340 --> 28:03.350
Ugh!

840
28:04.080 --> 28:05.130
You don't need to describe it anymore.

841
28:05.450 --> 28:06.560
Just take it out already.

842
28:07.180 --> 28:07.800
Alright.

843
28:08.760 --> 28:09.060
Oh!

844
28:09.060 --> 28:10.130
- Ow! - Whoa, whoa!

845
28:10.130 --> 28:10.880
Hey, hey, hey!

846
28:10.880 --> 28:12.570
- It bit me! - Help him!

847
28:12.570 --> 28:13.180
- Ouch... - Hey!

848
28:13.460 --> 28:14.300
Ow, help me!

849
28:20.960 --> 28:22.400
Ouch!

850
28:23.140 --> 28:23.750
Mr. Drip!

851
28:24.080 --> 28:24.950
Are you hurt, Mr. Drip?!

852
28:25.880 --> 28:26.580
Ugh!!

853
28:27.280 --> 28:28.800
It hurts because of you, Mr. Dolly!

854
28:30.250 --> 28:30.950
Hey, wait...

855
28:32.150 --> 28:34.210
Why does it look nothing like a dog bite?

856
28:34.210 --> 28:35.640
It looks like a human bite mark.

857
28:35.720 --> 28:36.330
Ugh!

858
28:37.250 --> 28:38.410
Well, I am a human!

859
28:39.160 --> 28:40.170
What the heck are you doing here?!

860
28:40.200 --> 28:40.760
Whoa...

861
28:40.760 --> 28:41.380
Huh?!

862
28:42.260 --> 28:42.820
Who?

863
28:42.820 --> 28:43.830
Who came up with this idea?

864
28:43.860 --> 28:44.780
- This guy right here. - He did.

865
28:48.770 --> 28:49.950
Come here, chubby.

866
28:50.290 --> 28:51.480
You'll take me to the hospital.

867
28:51.480 --> 28:51.880
Why?

868
28:51.880 --> 28:53.900
Your friend hurt my head lice!

869
28:54.530 --> 28:57.280
What did you do to my Mojo Dojo Casa House?

870
28:57.280 --> 28:58.780
I'm sorry... Mister...

871
28:58.780 --> 29:00.000
Do you know who I am?

872
29:00.000 --> 29:00.720
No?

873
29:00.720 --> 29:02.760
My name is Mister Hasamada Urukamahn

874
29:02.760 --> 29:03.610
An Incarnation

875
29:03.610 --> 29:04.460
Who Comes With Explosions

876
29:04.470 --> 29:05.460
John Weed Puller

877
29:05.460 --> 29:05.900
Da...

878
29:05.900 --> 29:06.800
Dafoe?

879
29:06.800 --> 29:07.520
Da hell.

880
29:07.520 --> 29:08.410
Whoa!

881
29:08.640 --> 29:09.310
- Come here. - Hey!

882
29:09.320 --> 29:10.330
- Wait, wait. - Hey!

883
29:10.340 --> 29:11.750
And who said I'm a poodle?

884
29:12.810 --> 29:13.930
I'm a Siberian husky!

885
29:13.930 --> 29:15.120
Whoa! Chill, bro!

886
29:16.500 --> 29:19.200
[The D Dorm]

887
29:19.570 --> 29:20.000
Ugh...

888
29:20.000 --> 29:21.800
Who is making noises so early in the morning?

889
29:24.020 --> 29:24.620
What?

890
29:25.090 --> 29:26.410
Good job, Auntie Duang.

891
29:27.050 --> 29:28.550
Why is she dancing here?

892
29:29.010 --> 29:30.220
We're trying to sleep here.

893
29:34.000 --> 29:35.950
I'm doing this for your sake.

894
29:36.080 --> 29:37.170
Since you said that...

895
29:37.170 --> 29:39.170
Grandpa's ghost liked to haunt you at night, right?

896
29:39.170 --> 29:40.630
You couldn't sleep at all, yeah?

897
29:40.810 --> 29:42.120
That's why I hired Auntie Duang

898
29:42.310 --> 29:43.780
to come dance for Grandpa's ghost,

899
29:43.980 --> 29:45.810
so he wouldn't disturb you at night.

900
29:46.770 --> 29:48.090
Gramps!

901
29:48.090 --> 29:50.480
Come watch me dance, and don't scare the kids, alright?

902
29:50.480 --> 29:51.920
- Yeah, I am watching you. - Understood?

903
29:51.920 --> 29:52.760
Got it.

904
29:52.760 --> 29:53.640
Leave.

905
29:53.640 --> 29:54.180
Shoo!

906
29:54.180 --> 29:54.950
Ow...

907
29:54.950 --> 29:56.620
- Shoo! - Keep going.

908
29:56.620 --> 29:57.820
- Shoo! - Ow!

909
29:57.820 --> 29:58.370
Good.

910
29:58.370 --> 29:59.750
Hey, Auntie!

911
30:00.080 --> 30:01.830
Are you trying to banish us instead of the ghost?!

912
30:02.150 --> 30:02.850
Would you like this, then?!

913
30:02.850 --> 30:04.400
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

914
30:05.100 --> 30:06.950
Are you trying to get back at us?

915
30:07.490 --> 30:08.600
Wow...

916
30:08.760 --> 30:10.700
That boy is always so jumpy.

917
30:10.700 --> 30:12.110
That boy is always so sippy.

918
30:12.520 --> 30:14.670
How are you not annoyed by each other?

919
30:15.350 --> 30:16.450
Hey, guys...

920
30:16.550 --> 30:18.550
If we really were trying to get back at you...

921
30:19.110 --> 30:20.900
What about it, then?

922
30:21.010 --> 30:21.960
Hm?!

923
30:21.960 --> 30:23.000
Now you'll understand

924
30:23.000 --> 30:24.240
how it feels like to be disturbed.

925
30:24.240 --> 30:26.200
I'll give you some advice. If you can't live like this,

926
30:26.200 --> 30:27.310
then leave!

927
30:27.310 --> 30:28.360
- All three of you. - Never!

928
30:29.300 --> 30:30.560
You are the ones that need to leave.

929
30:31.600 --> 30:32.840
Leave, leave, leave.

930
30:32.840 --> 30:33.890
- Go, go, go, go. - Whoa, whoa, whoa.

931
30:33.890 --> 30:34.540
Guys.

932
30:34.680 --> 30:35.750
- Hey, are you asking for trouble? - Go, go, go, go.

933
30:35.750 --> 30:36.810
How dare you hurt her?

934
30:36.810 --> 30:37.990
Whoever picks a fight with me,

935
30:38.000 --> 30:39.010
I don't discriminate.

936
30:39.010 --> 30:39.700
Hey, you can't do that.

937
30:39.700 --> 30:40.200
Step back.

938
30:40.200 --> 30:41.750
Hey, did you push my friend?

939
30:41.890 --> 30:43.350
- Would you like some of this, then?! - Whoa, don't do that. Hey!

940
30:43.360 --> 30:44.390
Bring it on!

941
30:47.320 --> 30:48.720
Whoa, Auntie Duang!

942
30:52.550 --> 30:53.700
- Hey! - Auntie Duang!

943
30:53.700 --> 30:54.520
Duang...

944
30:54.960 --> 30:55.740
Oh...

945
30:55.740 --> 30:56.430
Auntie Duang.

946
30:56.600 --> 30:57.760
Hey! Don't try to run away!

947
30:58.740 --> 30:59.330
Stop running...

948
30:59.750 --> 31:00.570
- Auntie Duang! - Duang!

949
31:00.570 --> 31:01.200
Hey!

950
31:01.930 --> 31:04.680
[The D Dorm]

951
31:06.420 --> 31:08.150
I couldn't focus on today's lessons at all.

952
31:08.910 --> 31:09.920
What about you guys?

953
31:10.660 --> 31:13.380
I just took a peek at Auntie Duang's restaurant.

954
31:13.380 --> 31:14.150
How was it?

955
31:14.150 --> 31:15.350
It was closed.

956
31:15.350 --> 31:16.010
Huh?

957
31:16.510 --> 31:17.500
It's never been closed before.

958
31:18.100 --> 31:18.840
Dape.

959
31:18.840 --> 31:19.380
Hm?

960
31:20.420 --> 31:21.860
Aren't you scared?

961
31:22.820 --> 31:23.750
Scared of what?

962
31:25.210 --> 31:26.500
If we insisted that

963
31:26.510 --> 31:27.750
we didn't push her

964
31:27.760 --> 31:29.120
and that she fell down on her own,

965
31:29.880 --> 31:33.170
the law would protect minors like us anyway, right?

966
31:37.300 --> 31:38.610
So cool.

967
31:39.780 --> 31:40.790
Besides,

968
31:41.890 --> 31:42.950
my father can always pull some strings

969
31:43.140 --> 31:44.520
and get us out of trouble.

970
31:44.850 --> 31:46.250
Yeah, that's true.

971
31:46.940 --> 31:48.460
I'm jealous of you, having a father like that.

972
31:48.700 --> 31:50.400
He's super-duper cool.

973
31:51.050 --> 31:52.060
That's great, bro.

974
31:52.320 --> 31:53.340
- Mm. - Of course.

975
31:53.710 --> 31:54.730
Come on, let's get on with our band practice.

976
31:54.730 --> 31:55.830
Hey, guys...

977
31:55.830 --> 31:56.570
Hm?

978
31:56.930 --> 31:58.220
What is that in front of our room?

979
31:58.900 --> 31:59.750
Go take a look, won't you?

980
32:03.560 --> 32:04.370
What?

981
32:04.370 --> 32:06.370
[You are cordially invited to the bathing rite of Mrs. Duangjai Rungthiwahong (Auntie Duang)]

982
32:06.370 --> 32:08.400
Auntie Duang is dead?!

983
32:09.840 --> 32:10.620
Sh*t!

984
32:10.740 --> 32:11.750
Dape, it's your fault!

985
32:12.620 --> 32:13.360
Auntie Duang is dead...

986
32:13.360 --> 32:14.150
Did we kill her?

987
32:14.150 --> 32:15.350
What are you afraid of?

988
32:15.520 --> 32:17.020
I told you. We won't be punished.

989
32:17.040 --> 32:18.830
But Auntie Duang died for real, though.

990
32:19.450 --> 32:20.780
Listen to me.

991
32:21.060 --> 32:24.150
"Juvenile offenders can never be severely punished."

992
32:25.580 --> 32:27.730
If they're going to punish us, my father can take care of it.

993
32:27.840 --> 32:29.240
We won't get thrown in jail.

994
32:33.870 --> 32:34.820
Whoa!

995
32:35.500 --> 32:36.410
Whoa!

996
32:38.860 --> 32:39.690
Whoa!

997
32:39.690 --> 32:40.550
Whoa!

998
32:40.920 --> 32:41.580
Whoa!

999
32:41.580 --> 32:43.450
Who the hell put Thai music on?!

1000
32:43.710 --> 32:45.160
Is it Auntie Duang's ghost?!

1001
32:45.490 --> 32:47.170
Ugh, stop making such a fuss!

1002
32:48.400 --> 32:49.490
Who is behind this?!

1003
32:49.490 --> 32:50.440
Show yourself!

1004
32:51.140 --> 32:51.660
There...

1005
32:51.660 --> 32:53.120
There she comes...

1006
32:53.130 --> 32:54.000
Dape...

1007
32:54.820 --> 32:56.660
You can stay here if you want!

1008
32:56.960 --> 32:57.960
We're...

1009
32:57.960 --> 32:58.810
leaving!

1010
33:00.370 --> 33:01.150
Come back here.

1011
33:02.530 --> 33:03.370
Come back.

1012
33:04.410 --> 33:05.570
Come back here!

1013
33:11.520 --> 33:12.950
If you're not coming back...

1014
33:14.540 --> 33:15.690
then wait for me.

1015
33:16.090 --> 33:17.210
Wait for me!

1016
33:19.300 --> 33:20.020
Whoa...

1017
33:20.150 --> 33:21.650
Why did you guys stop?

1018
33:23.120 --> 33:24.370
Look...

1019
33:24.370 --> 33:25.350
- Whoa! - Auntie Duang's ghost...

1020
33:26.000 --> 33:27.000
Auntie Duang's ghost...

1021
33:31.720 --> 33:33.200
Auntie, I'm sorry!

1022
33:34.250 --> 33:35.920
These two pushed you down the stairs.

1023
33:35.920 --> 33:36.650
- Huh? - Huh?

1024
33:37.520 --> 33:38.150
I didn't do it.

1025
33:38.150 --> 33:39.160
I was drinking...

1026
33:39.160 --> 33:40.940
I was drinking a cola, Auntie.

1027
33:41.300 --> 33:42.850
Dope! What are you saying?

1028
33:43.090 --> 33:45.040
You guys apologize to Auntie right now!

1029
33:46.040 --> 33:47.170
I... I have nothing to do with this.

1030
33:47.170 --> 33:48.020
I'm going that way.

1031
33:48.340 --> 33:49.640
Hey, I'm coming with you!

1032
33:53.200 --> 33:53.740
What?

1033
33:53.750 --> 33:54.830
What? Why did you stop?

1034
33:55.540 --> 33:57.040
She doesn't have a head...

1035
34:00.240 --> 34:00.950
Dump,

1036
34:01.220 --> 34:02.320
you like jumping at people, right?

1037
34:02.520 --> 34:03.180
Huh?

1038
34:03.350 --> 34:04.550
Bring it on!

1039
34:05.100 --> 34:06.370
Don't!

1040
34:07.050 --> 34:08.139
Bring it on!

1041
34:08.150 --> 34:09.389
Don't bring it on!

1042
34:09.800 --> 34:10.409
Ugh...

1043
34:10.620 --> 34:12.010
Bring it on! Come on!

1044
34:12.010 --> 34:13.300
Don't!

1045
34:13.610 --> 34:14.980
Don't...

1046
34:16.210 --> 34:17.699
I'll get there myself!

1047
34:24.949 --> 34:25.960
I'm... I'm sorry.

1048
34:26.290 --> 34:26.850
I'm sorry...

1049
34:26.850 --> 34:27.350
I...

1050
34:29.750 --> 34:30.949
I... I didn't mean to do it.

1051
34:30.949 --> 34:33.199
Dump... Dump bumped into me.

1052
34:33.350 --> 34:33.909
What?

1053
34:33.909 --> 34:34.929
Why the hell are you blaming me?!

1054
34:34.940 --> 34:36.010
Auntie, listen...

1055
34:36.010 --> 34:37.330
He's the worst.

1056
34:37.340 --> 34:39.010
He said we'd never get sent to jail

1057
34:39.010 --> 34:40.550
because we're juvenile offenders.

1058
34:40.679 --> 34:42.070
Even if we went to jail, his father would help us out.

1059
34:42.070 --> 34:43.179
Break his neck, Auntie!

1060
34:43.320 --> 34:44.699
Snap it!

1061
34:44.699 --> 34:46.219
Snap his neck...

1062
34:46.400 --> 34:48.350
I'll kill you all!

1063
34:48.480 --> 34:49.130
Don't!

1064
34:49.130 --> 34:50.370
- No! - Don't!

1065
34:51.010 --> 34:52.139
- No... - No! Don't!

1066
34:54.520 --> 34:56.610
We're doomed.

1067
34:56.610 --> 34:58.040
We're done for...

1068
34:58.040 --> 34:59.750
Tada!

1069
34:59.920 --> 35:02.190
Auntie Duang is not dead, you minors.

1070
35:07.420 --> 35:08.410
Tada!

1071
35:08.410 --> 35:09.190
Whoa!

1072
35:16.090 --> 35:17.300
Humans are better than ghosts

1073
35:17.330 --> 35:19.240
when it comes to scaring fellow humans, huh?

1074
35:20.930 --> 35:22.590
You pranked us?!

1075
35:25.920 --> 35:27.680
I won't let this slide.

1076
35:27.940 --> 35:30.500
I'll have my father close your dorm down!

1077
35:34.440 --> 35:38.520
[The D Dorm]

1078
35:39.220 --> 35:41.360
I already took care of the ingredients that would expire soon.

1079
35:42.370 --> 35:43.730
Get some rest, Mr. Drip.

1080
35:43.730 --> 35:44.870
Don't worry about the cafe.

1081
35:45.220 --> 35:46.630
Focus on your recovery for now.

1082
35:47.640 --> 35:48.380
Yes.

1083
35:50.620 --> 35:51.350
By the way...

1084
35:52.280 --> 35:53.290
Mr. Dobby and the others...

1085
35:53.300 --> 35:55.720
They didn't prank those kids too harshly, did they?

1086
35:57.240 --> 35:58.750
They deserved worse than that

1087
35:59.320 --> 36:01.010
for pushing my mom down the stairs.

1088
36:01.570 --> 36:03.580
She's lucky that she has a very flexible

1089
36:03.580 --> 36:05.240
and stout body with a thick neck,

1090
36:05.240 --> 36:06.450
so she wasn't severely injured.

1091
36:06.450 --> 36:07.870
A stout body with a thick neck?

1092
36:08.600 --> 36:09.940
Your mother has a funny body shape.

1093
36:09.940 --> 36:10.530
Hey!

1094
36:10.530 --> 36:11.240
Just like me...

1095
36:12.230 --> 36:12.950
It's alright.

1096
36:13.600 --> 36:15.350
Hey, about what you said earlier, you don't have to worry.

1097
36:15.350 --> 36:16.180
Mr. Dollar was there, too.

1098
36:16.180 --> 36:18.090
He wouldn't let them get hurt.

1099
36:18.090 --> 36:18.720
That's right...

1100
36:19.120 --> 36:20.150
The person you should

1101
36:20.320 --> 36:21.310
be worried about is Mr. Drip.

1102
36:21.990 --> 36:23.660
He fell down a sewer while running from that madman.

1103
36:24.020 --> 36:25.760
I can't say when he'll be able to open the cafe again.

1104
36:26.380 --> 36:27.140
Are you worried about him?

1105
36:32.380 --> 36:33.410
Ahem...

1106
36:33.740 --> 36:34.250
Oh...

1107
36:35.290 --> 36:35.860
- I got it! - Whoa!

1108
36:35.870 --> 36:36.470
Whoa...

1109
36:36.990 --> 36:38.000
A black dog's tears.

1110
36:38.500 --> 36:40.670
Don't tell me you fought a dog for that?

1111
36:41.430 --> 36:42.260
Ugh...

1112
36:42.260 --> 36:43.370
Why were you so hell-bent on getting that?

1113
36:43.530 --> 36:44.610
This time,

1114
36:44.960 --> 36:46.140
I'll finally be able to see ghosts.

1115
36:48.800 --> 36:49.600
- Hey... - Oh, oh.

1116
36:50.600 --> 36:51.170
Whoa...

1117
36:58.880 --> 36:59.750
Gah...

1118
37:00.040 --> 37:00.950
- Whoa. - Gah...

1119
37:01.210 --> 37:02.570
I think it worked. He's seeing something.

1120
37:02.590 --> 37:03.700
- Gah! - "Gramps"?

1121
37:03.700 --> 37:04.700
Where is he?

1122
37:06.950 --> 37:07.760
It burns!

1123
37:07.760 --> 37:08.150
What?

1124
37:08.150 --> 37:08.860
What?

1125
37:08.860 --> 37:10.380
Hey, he needs some water.

1126
37:10.380 --> 37:11.370
- Help him... - I'll help.

1127
37:11.370 --> 37:12.270
What's wrong?

1128
37:12.270 --> 37:13.280
Take me to the doctor...

1129
37:13.780 --> 37:14.920
Don't touch me! Move!

1130
37:21.500 --> 37:24.700
I want to see what their parents look like.

1131
37:24.700 --> 37:26.150
These kids...

1132
37:26.150 --> 37:27.680
How were they even raised

1133
37:27.680 --> 37:30.680
to become such a menace to society?

1134
37:31.140 --> 37:31.850
Who?!

1135
37:32.400 --> 37:33.350
Who did this?!

1136
37:37.220 --> 37:39.220
Who dared pick on my son?

1137
37:39.460 --> 37:40.010
Huh?

1138
37:40.550 --> 37:41.380
Wow...

1139
37:41.750 --> 37:43.220
Acting all high and mighty.

1140
37:43.490 --> 37:45.350
No wonder your son turned out that way.

1141
37:49.220 --> 37:50.000
What even are you?

1142
37:50.290 --> 37:50.970
A kappa.

1143
37:50.970 --> 37:51.630
I'm not leaving.

1144
37:51.630 --> 37:52.550
I just got here.

1145
37:53.210 --> 37:54.950
Everyone here

1146
37:55.340 --> 37:57.110
humiliated my son.

1147
37:57.490 --> 37:58.550
You'll have to be responsible for this!

1148
37:59.600 --> 38:01.620
Tell Uncle Danai who owns this dorm to come talk to me.

1149
38:03.710 --> 38:05.200
You know my Grandpa?

1150
38:05.790 --> 38:06.990
Stop talking

1151
38:07.330 --> 38:09.110
and bring him here already!

1152
38:10.640 --> 38:11.730
Surachet?

1153
38:12.050 --> 38:12.720
Is it...

1154
38:12.840 --> 38:14.580
Is it really you...?

1155
38:16.400 --> 38:17.750
My Grandpa passed away.

1156
38:18.400 --> 38:19.600
I'm now in charge of this property.

1157
38:19.860 --> 38:20.920
You can talk to me.

1158
38:21.110 --> 38:23.310
These kids were just a bit too loud.

1159
38:23.560 --> 38:25.260
Just a warning should've been enough,

1160
38:25.620 --> 38:27.820
but you tried to scare them with ghosts.

1161
38:28.100 --> 38:30.540
If my son had a heart attack,

1162
38:30.770 --> 38:31.760
who would be responsible for that?!

1163
38:32.720 --> 38:33.710
Yes, Dad.

1164
38:34.210 --> 38:35.050
I was scared...

1165
38:36.240 --> 38:37.380
I was so scared.

1166
38:40.680 --> 38:41.750
But your son

1167
38:42.530 --> 38:43.840
pushed my mom down the stairs.

1168
38:45.350 --> 38:46.880
If something happened to her,

1169
38:47.540 --> 38:48.580
who would be responsible for that?

1170
38:49.190 --> 38:50.040
Yes, Dear.

1171
38:50.310 --> 38:51.160
I was scared...

1172
38:51.350 --> 38:52.860
I was so scared.

1173
38:52.860 --> 38:53.750
Ugh...

1174
38:53.910 --> 38:56.080
You're the scariest person right now.

1175
38:56.520 --> 38:57.220
Hey...

1176
39:00.270 --> 39:02.150
Why is he drinking that all day?

1177
39:02.150 --> 39:03.080
When did he even get a refill?

1178
39:03.350 --> 39:04.550
Auntie,

1179
39:04.630 --> 39:06.500
- I apologize on my son's behalf... - Shut up!

1180
39:06.500 --> 39:07.120
You...

1181
39:10.200 --> 39:11.420
Shut your stupid mouth.

1182
39:11.790 --> 39:12.800
Keep your nose out of this.

1183
39:14.820 --> 39:15.960
Surachet...

1184
39:16.780 --> 39:17.750
You...

1185
39:28.060 --> 39:29.360
How did you know that

1186
39:29.820 --> 39:32.860
my son was the one who pushed that auntie, huh?

1187
39:33.760 --> 39:35.090
My son...

1188
39:35.620 --> 39:36.760
is a good kid.

1189
39:37.250 --> 39:38.320
That's true.

1190
39:39.160 --> 39:39.880
I...

1191
39:40.050 --> 39:41.390
I couldn't even bring myself to step on some ants.

1192
39:42.480 --> 39:43.400
Yesterday...

1193
39:43.800 --> 39:46.070
I saw an ant nest in the water.

1194
39:47.170 --> 39:49.850
I...scooped the ants up slowly

1195
39:49.850 --> 39:51.350
one by one.

1196
39:52.740 --> 39:54.050
It took me an hour

1197
39:54.250 --> 39:55.650
to save every single ant.

1198
39:57.180 --> 39:59.210
Why would you save just one of them at a time?

1199
39:59.210 --> 40:00.440
Why not just pick up the whole nest?

1200
40:01.600 --> 40:02.150
Ow...

1201
40:03.740 --> 40:04.840
There's one of them here.

1202
40:07.190 --> 40:08.150
Be quiet

1203
40:08.680 --> 40:09.690
and keep your mouth shut.

1204
40:12.360 --> 40:13.920
You said that your son was a good person.

1205
40:15.140 --> 40:16.140
We have evidence against that.

1206
40:17.260 --> 40:18.040
Where is it?

1207
40:18.400 --> 40:19.210
Here.

1208
40:26.420 --> 40:28.550
♫Kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss♫

1209
40:28.550 --> 40:29.750
♫This kiss is for you♫

1210
40:30.300 --> 40:33.000
- ♫Kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss♫ - Uh... Sorry.

1211
40:33.030 --> 40:34.400
- Uh... - Hey... Do it properly.

1212
40:34.550 --> 40:35.560
You went along with it, too.

1213
40:36.940 --> 40:37.330
Here.

1214
40:37.330 --> 40:38.150
I'm sorry!

1215
40:38.150 --> 40:39.350
I... I didn't mean to do it.

1216
40:39.350 --> 40:41.710
Dump... Dump bumped into me...

1217
40:41.710 --> 40:42.220
What?

1218
40:42.230 --> 40:43.150
Why the hell are you blaming me?!

1219
40:43.330 --> 40:44.150
Auntie, listen...

1220
40:44.150 --> 40:45.840
He's the worst.

1221
40:45.840 --> 40:47.320
He said we'd never get sent to jail

1222
40:47.320 --> 40:48.890
because we're juvenile offenders.

1223
40:48.890 --> 40:50.380
Even if we went to jail, his father would help us out.

1224
40:50.380 --> 40:51.640
Break his neck, Auntie!

1225
40:51.640 --> 40:53.000
Snap it!!

1226
40:53.000 --> 40:54.950
Snap his neck...

1227
40:58.800 --> 40:59.380
Alright.

1228
41:00.580 --> 41:02.150
If my son is actually in the wrong...

1229
41:03.230 --> 41:03.900
Alright, then.

1230
41:04.550 --> 41:05.750
What do you want?

1231
41:06.640 --> 41:07.840
A flower basket?

1232
41:08.410 --> 41:09.420
Money?

1233
41:10.140 --> 41:11.290
What do you want?

1234
41:11.750 --> 41:12.180
Hm?

1235
41:13.430 --> 41:14.980
I want your son to know that

1236
41:16.700 --> 41:17.840
being a minor

1237
41:18.350 --> 41:19.920
means you'll have more chances in court.

1238
41:20.550 --> 41:22.640
It doesn't allow you to get away without repercussions.

1239
41:24.280 --> 41:27.080
And since you, his parents, couldn't teach him that,

1240
41:28.200 --> 41:29.700
I'll let the law be his teacher.

1241
41:31.130 --> 41:33.220
Ooh!

1242
41:33.350 --> 41:34.970
It's not every day

1243
41:34.970 --> 41:37.040
that you talk like a police officer.

1244
41:37.840 --> 41:39.590
I only see you dance in the community.

1245
41:39.740 --> 41:41.530
Wiggle, wiggle, wiggle...

1246
41:41.530 --> 41:42.210
- Wiggle... - That's true, Mom.

1247
41:42.210 --> 41:42.810
Yeah.

1248
41:43.180 --> 41:43.810
Alright, Mom.

1249
41:44.180 --> 41:44.840
Let's go to the police station.

1250
41:45.200 --> 41:45.710
Wait.

1251
41:45.710 --> 41:46.650
I was just teasing you,

1252
41:46.800 --> 41:48.050
now you're arresting me?

1253
41:48.050 --> 41:49.280
You'll testify at the station.

1254
41:49.280 --> 41:50.370
Oh. Umm...

1255
41:51.350 --> 41:51.760
How would I know...?

1256
41:51.760 --> 41:53.100
Please come to

1257
41:53.360 --> 41:54.260
the police station.

1258
41:57.220 --> 41:58.200
You guys, too.

1259
41:58.550 --> 41:59.090
Come on.

1260
42:05.530 --> 42:06.560
Follow me.

1261
42:06.560 --> 42:07.460
Come here.

1262
42:07.600 --> 42:08.150
Go.

1263
42:12.200 --> 42:13.580
Why didn't you ask if I wanted a drink?

1264
42:13.580 --> 42:14.590
Ask me, too.

1265
42:15.000 --> 42:15.760
Is it good?

1266
42:16.250 --> 42:17.750
- I want to drink it, too. - Hey, don't play along.

1267
42:17.880 --> 42:18.220
What...?

1268
42:18.220 --> 42:19.580
- Let them go to the police station. - But he didn't invite...

1269
42:20.150 --> 42:21.950
Our dorm is finally

1270
42:21.950 --> 42:23.530
peaceful.

1271
42:23.530 --> 42:24.040
Yay...

1272
42:24.400 --> 42:25.900
Thank you, everyone,

1273
42:25.900 --> 42:27.350
for this Auntie Duang's ghost plan.

1274
42:27.860 --> 42:29.980
Apart from Guard Dum, you're the only one

1275
42:29.980 --> 42:31.380
who could come up with such an evil plan.

1276
42:31.380 --> 42:32.000
That's right.

1277
42:32.260 --> 42:33.700
Of course, it's only natural...

1278
42:33.700 --> 42:34.370
Hey, wait.

1279
42:34.990 --> 42:36.000
Was that a compliment?

1280
42:36.580 --> 42:37.080
Well...

1281
42:37.080 --> 42:38.850
It's up to your interpretation.

1282
42:39.350 --> 42:40.090
You complimented me, right?

1283
42:40.430 --> 42:41.250
- You did, right? - Maybe.

1284
42:41.250 --> 42:41.980
Maybe I did.

1285
42:44.150 --> 42:45.340
Those kids deserved it.

1286
42:45.370 --> 42:46.240
- Dobby. - Hm?

1287
42:46.650 --> 42:47.560
How did...

1288
42:47.560 --> 42:49.340
Surachet and Gramps know each other?

1289
42:50.150 --> 42:50.900
Oh, you're right.

1290
42:51.160 --> 42:52.370
- Right... - I was curious about that, too.

1291
42:52.870 --> 42:53.750
Let me ask him.

1292
42:54.010 --> 42:54.950
Grandpa!

1293
42:54.950 --> 42:55.500
What?

1294
42:55.720 --> 42:56.610
Grandpa!

1295
42:56.970 --> 42:57.980
Where did he go?

1296
42:59.180 --> 43:00.400
Serves you right.

1297
43:00.520 --> 43:01.860
You were doing just fine

1298
43:02.040 --> 43:03.850
before you applied those dog tears to your eyes.

1299
43:04.260 --> 43:05.240
Those were full of germs.

1300
43:05.530 --> 43:06.080
You know what?

1301
43:06.080 --> 43:07.260
It should have made you blind.

1302
43:07.260 --> 43:08.890
That would stop your obsession with seeing ghosts.

1303
43:11.260 --> 43:12.610
If you're not going to help, then go away.

1304
43:12.820 --> 43:14.150
Stop complaining. It's annoying!

1305
43:15.250 --> 43:16.550
You're the one to talk.

1306
43:16.650 --> 43:18.160
You were whimpering like a dog,

1307
43:19.280 --> 43:19.860
"Ow!

1308
43:20.150 --> 43:21.180
It burns.

